      "id": "6uz22o8",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "1. Levels of Organization in the Human Body"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "The human body is structured through distinct levels of organization, starting from cells to tissues, organs, and organ systems.",
        "The Circulatory and Respiratory systems collaborate to deliver oxygen and essential nutrients while removing carbon dioxide.",
        "Metabolic waste elimination and nutrient processing are primarily driven by the Excretory and Digestive systems.",
        "Coordination across all body functions is jointly managed by the Nervous System (rapid electrical impulses) and the Endocrine System (hormonal regulation)."
      ],
      "id": "f8tt63r"
    },
